# Generated dashboard output
dashboard.html
# ...but the Snowflake Summit dashboard ships its built HTML as the deliverable.
!snowflake_summit/dashboard.html
# ...and the Competitive Landscape sibling ships its built HTML the same way.
!landscape/dashboard.html
# Local convenience copy of the built dashboard. Some setups copy/symlink
# dashboard.html -> index.html to preview at file://.../index.html. The
# PUBLIC site never uses a tracked root index.html: pages.yml regenerates
# from app.py and writes _site/index.html from dashboard.html, and server.py
# serves "/" by live-rendering via dash.render_html(). Ignore so a local
# copy is never recommitted. Anchored to the root: every sub-site page
# (lthcs_tab/index.html, health/index.html, ...) is source and must stay
# addable without `git add -f`.
/index.html
# The Pages staging tree. pages.yml's "Stage site directory" step builds this
# and hands it to upload-pages-artifact; nothing in it is source. Reproducing
# the staging locally to measure the artifact leaves ~679MB of copied data
# here (data/lthcs alone is staged twice), so it must never be commit-able.
_site/
# Lazy-loaded sidecar payloads (whale, etc.) — written by app.py next to
# dashboard.html on every build. Same lifecycle as the HTML itself.
data-*.json
# Carve-out: data-travel.json IS committed, as a floor. Every build refreshes
# it in place from travel.state.gov (app.py -> fetch_advisories.py) and never
# commits it back. When the scrape fails outright the fetcher keeps the prior
# file, which therefore has to exist at checkout. (As of 2026-10 the State
# Dept HTML pages answer 403 to our runners; the RSS fallback still rebuilds
# the advisories, without risk codes.)
!data-travel.json
# Carve-out: data-us_states.json is committed STATIC geometry — 50 states + DC
# SVG paths (pre-projected Albers USA) built once by
# scripts/build_us_state_paths.py from us-atlas. Consumed by the V1 Real Estate
# tab's geographic heat map. Refreshed essentially never (boundaries don't move).
!data-us_states.json
# Carve-out: data-city.json IS committed — the City tab's sidecar, refreshed
# daily by city-daily.yml (mirrors data/real_estate.json's committed-data model)
# so the V1 build always has city data even on a cold CI checkout.
!data-city.json
# Carve-out: data-stock-money-flow.json (Stock Flows tab) stays committed only
# as an empty cold-checkout floor (as_of 2026-06-08, 0 stocks). The real file is
# written inside pages.yml's fetch-market step on every build (fetch_market ->
# fetch_stock_money_flow.build_from_signals) and deployed from there, never
# committed back; the daily workflow that used to commit it was deleted on
# 2026-06-08. scripts/data_health.py still classifies it as COMMITTED, so
# reclassify it there before dropping this floor.
!data-stock-money-flow.json
# Carve-out: data-aviation.json IS committed — the Aviation tab's static sidecar
# (FAA airman/registry data, used-market snapshot, live seed). Refreshed by hand.
!data-aviation.json
# Carve-out: data-cfpb.json IS committed — the CFPB complaint feed refreshed daily
# by cfpb-daily.yml. Consumed by the ADW Worker (ADW-397) via fetchAlpineFeed('cfpb')
# because the CFPB API blocks Cloudflare datacenter IPs; GitHub Actions has clean
# egress. Committed so the feed exists on a cold checkout / first publish.
!data-cfpb.json
# Carve-out: data-usaspending.json IS committed — the USAspending obligation feed
# refreshed daily by usaspending-daily.yml. Consumed by the ADW Worker (ADW-441 and
# ADW-444) via fetchAlpineFeed('usaspending') because the USAspending API blocks
# Cloudflare datacenter IPs; GitHub Actions has clean egress. Committed so the feed
# exists on a cold checkout / first publish.
!data-usaspending.json
# Carve-out: data-tsa.json IS committed — the Aviation tab's TSA Throughput
# sub-view sidecar, refreshed daily by aviation-tsa.yml (fetch_tsa.py). The
# client falls back to the baked-in seed (DATA.aviation.tsa.seed) if absent.
!data-tsa.json
# Carve-out: data-opensky.json IS committed — the Aviation tab's live OpenSky
# "airborne now" snapshot, refreshed hourly by aviation-opensky.yml.
!data-opensky.json
# Built by pages.yml at deploy time, never committed: data-opensky-positions.json (data-*.json above) and
health/api-catalog.xlsx
# Carve-out: data-mufon.json IS committed — the UAP tab's sidecar. It's refreshed
# live by the V2 build each deploy, but committing a snapshot gives a stale-keep
# fallback so a V2-build timeout (NUFORC backfill) can't 404 the MUFON tab.
!data-mufon.json
# Carve-out: data-city.schema.json is a hand-authored CONTRACT (not a generated
# sidecar), loaded by the City Pulse conformance tests (tests/test_city_pulse.py).
# The data-*.json rule above matches it by name and was silently keeping it out of
# git — which is why those tests FileNotFound in CI. Un-ignore so it ships.
!docs/city/data-city.schema.json
# V2 builder output mirrors the production layout one level down.
v2/dashboard.html
v2/data-*.json
# Same carve-out for V2's sidecar — see comment above data-travel.json.
!v2/data-travel.json

# Local cached fetches stay on your machine (regenerated every run)
data/*.json
data/*.bak
data/*.farside-vertical.bak
# Stale-fallback cache for flaky third-party APIs (FRED/Glassnode/mempool/Etherscan)
data/.stale/*
# ...except the NUFORC per-month subndx caches: committing the ~144 backfill
# months lets fetch_mufon refresh only {today_ym, prior_ym} in CI instead of
# re-fetching ~240 months from scratch, which kept blowing the V2 build's
# timeout before fetch_stock_prices could run.
!data/.stale/nuforc_subndx_*.json
# Central monitoring snapshot — regenerated by scripts/build_health_status.py
# each CI run before staging. Local copies are throwaway.
#
# Written as `data/health/*` rather than `data/health/`: git does not descend
# into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a `!data/health/…` carve-out under a trailing-
# slash rule is silently inert. The glob form keeps the contents ignored while
# leaving the directory itself visible, which is what makes the exception below
# actually work. Do not "tidy" it back to `data/health/`.
data/health/*
# ...except the API status record. DELIBERATELY UN-IGNORED, and the reasoning
# matters: data/health/status.json above it is a build CACHE — recomputed from
# scratch every run out of files already in the repo, so committing it would
# just be storing a derivation. api_status.json is a RECORD. It is the only
# artifact of a live sweep of ~50 third-party endpoints at one moment in time,
# and that moment cannot be reconstructed later from anything in this
# repository. Ignoring it meant the authoritative per-API status existed for
# exactly one build and was then destroyed with the runner: no `git log`, no
# diff, no way to answer "when did Census start 403ing?" without having
# happened to load the deployed page that hour.
#
# pages.yml's "Commit the API status record" step commits it back, guarded so a
# failed or structurally empty probe can never replace a good record with
# nothing, and rate-limited so an unchanged record is not re-committed hourly.
!data/health/api_status.json
# NOTE: data/*.csv (ETF flow history) is intentionally NOT ignored — those
# files are tracked so the public dashboard can ship real flow data.
# Update them locally via the dashboard's "Paste CSV…" workflow, then commit.

# Keep schema templates if you want to re-add them later (manually)
!data/.gitkeep
# Hand-curated AI-funding seed list, read by fetch_market.load_ai_curated()
# (the Wikipedia-enriched copy, data/ai_curated_wiki.json, stays ignored).
!data/ai_curated.json
# US real-estate snapshot — committed back by real-estate-daily.yml and read
# by the /real-estate/ page. Updates daily; tracked so the public page works.
!data/real_estate.json
# Metro centroid coords from Census CBSA gazetteer — built by
# scripts/fetch_metro_coords.py, read by the /real-estate/ heat map.
# Rarely changes (annual Census release); tracked so the page works.
!data/metro_coords.json

# LTHCS — local API response cache (raw vendor data, may have redistribution terms)
.cache/

# Local env / secrets
.env
.env.local
*.local

# Claude Code local config, skills and worktrees — kept out of this public repo
# (worktrees are transient parallel-agent scratch space; the branch is the deliverable).
.claude/

# Snowflake Summit vendor enrichment (generated by enrich_vendors.py)
snowflake_summit/.enrich_cache.json
snowflake_summit/enrichment.json

# One-off backfill validation dumps from May 2026; nothing reads them.
data/lthcs/backfill_validation_*.json

# Deploy-time LTHCS indexes written by scripts/build_lthcs_site_index.py in
# pages.yml (derived from the committed data on every deploy; never commit).
data/lthcs/file_index.json
data/lthcs/health_summary.json
data/lthcs/history/pillars_by_ticker/
data/lthcs/history/trend_index.json
